# Pharos backend + auth keys. Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in, or set as
# EAS secrets for cloud builds. When SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are present
# the app runs against Supabase (Sign in with Apple + email/password); otherwise
# it falls back to a local dev store (so it still runs in Expo Go without keys).
# See docs/BACKEND-SETUP.md for where each value comes from.

# Supabase project (Settings → API)
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Server-side only — do NOT put these here / in app.config.ts ───────────────
# In-app feedback creates Linear tickets via the `submit-feedback` Edge Function.
# The Linear key is a SECRET and must live only in the Edge Function environment,
# never bundled into the client. Set them on Supabase, not in this file:
#   supabase secrets set LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_xxxx LINEAR_TEAM_ID=<team-uuid>
# LINEAR_TEAM_ID is the target Linear team (feedback lands there).
